WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.893
Tutorial two.

00:00:00.893 --> 00:00:02.817
Rules and stage progression.

00:00:02.817 --> 00:00:07.969
Open Competition, then Tournaments and rules, and choose the correct event.

00:00:07.969 --> 00:00:14.564
In Overview and schedule, set the game, start date, registration deadline and tournament status.

00:00:14.564 --> 00:00:16.213
Dates use Malaysia time.

00:00:16.213 --> 00:00:20.197
Registration and public results are controlled separately.

00:00:20.197 --> 00:00:24.800
Check that you are configuring the correct SOLO or TEAM tournament.

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:28.480
Open Sizes and updates, then Change tournament sizes.

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:35.005
Set the capacities, league rounds, matches per player, qualification places and bracket sizes.

00:00:35.005 --> 00:00:40.143
Under Series lengths, choose the league, knockout and final match lengths.

00:00:40.143 --> 00:00:44.864
For example, use best of five for knockout and best of seven for the

00:00:44.864 --> 00:00:45.280
final.

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:48.682
All lengths must be odd, from one to ninety nine.

00:00:48.682 --> 00:00:53.473
Fill the eligible player slots and complete four-player team rosters.

00:00:53.473 --> 00:00:58.610
Generate and check the SOLO league fixtures, then confirm the player list.

00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:00.214
Open Rules and stages.

00:01:00.214 --> 00:01:03.786
On each stage card, select Edit tournament rules.

00:01:03.786 --> 00:01:06.701
Choose match points and the draw policy.

00:01:06.701 --> 00:01:14.720
Set league tiebreakers, qualification length, starting points, opponents, and playoff tiebreakers where shown.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:19.166
For knockout, confirm the player or team starting-order rule.

00:01:19.166 --> 00:01:22.592
Set forfeits and screenshot and dispute timing.

00:01:22.592 --> 00:01:25.071
Scroll down and select Save rules.

00:01:25.071 --> 00:01:29.517
Saving confirms filled choices; blank rules remain undecided.

00:01:29.517 --> 00:01:31.850
Repeat for every relevant stage.

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:33.506
Review Ready to publish.

00:01:33.506 --> 00:01:37.647
Select each incomplete item to open the relevant setup task.

00:01:37.647 --> 00:01:43.858
Complete the required dates, rules, eligibility, rosters, player-list and schedule checks.

00:01:43.858 --> 00:01:50.138
Choose an active tournament status, then select Publish tournament when every check passes.

00:01:50.138 --> 00:01:52.830
Draft and Archived cannot be published.

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:55.659
Unpublishing retains players and history.

00:01:55.659 --> 00:02:01.180
Changes to a published or started event may require an admin-controlled restart.

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:04.424
After league play, confirm all required matches.

00:02:04.424 --> 00:02:08.883
Every player must have the configured number of finalized results.

00:02:08.883 --> 00:02:12.397
On the league card, select Manage stage progression.

00:02:12.397 --> 00:02:14.627
Review the final player rankings.

00:02:14.627 --> 00:02:17.465
Select a player's name to inspect results.

00:02:17.465 --> 00:02:23.141
Use arrows only to resolve remaining ties under the confirmed rules, and explain the

00:02:23.141 --> 00:02:23.750
decision.

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:27.263
Do not reverse points or a confirmed tiebreak order.

00:02:27.263 --> 00:02:30.980
Select Save final rankings to freeze the current order.

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:37.293
For qualification, first save its rules and confirm the starting-points choice: start from zero

00:02:37.293 --> 00:02:38.756
or keep league points.

00:02:38.756 --> 00:02:40.749
Open Manage stage progression.

00:02:40.749 --> 00:02:45.069
With automatic opponents, select Auto assign and create fixtures.

00:02:45.069 --> 00:02:50.452
With manual opponents, choose each pair and select Create qualification fixtures.

00:02:50.452 --> 00:02:56.168
Use the playoff pool from the frozen league ranking, with distinct opponents and equal

00:02:56.168 --> 00:02:58.161
configured matches per player.

00:02:58.161 --> 00:03:01.750
Existing qualification fixtures cannot be overwritten.

00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:04.670
Score and confirm all qualification matches.

00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:10.244
Review its standings, resolve remaining ties with a reason, and save final rankings.

00:03:10.244 --> 00:03:16.349
Direct qualifiers and the configured top playoff finishers now form the SOLO knockout field.

00:03:16.349 --> 00:03:21.724
On the knockout card, confirm the pairing rule and open Manage stage progression.

00:03:21.724 --> 00:03:28.294
Review the complete starting order when using manual seeding, then select Create confirmed bracket.

00:03:28.294 --> 00:03:32.010
Check the first-round opponents in Fixtures and results.

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:34.308
TEAM follows its own knockout path.

00:03:34.308 --> 00:03:40.676
Complete every configured team with four eligible players, and save the TEAM starting-order rule.

00:03:40.676 --> 00:03:45.994
On the TEAM card, open Manage stage progression, arrange the full team order, and

00:03:45.994 --> 00:03:48.095
select Create confirmed bracket.

00:03:48.095 --> 00:03:51.444
Review the pairings and any configured seeded byes.

00:03:51.444 --> 00:03:55.580
TEAM progression does not depend on completing the SOLO league.

00:03:55.580 --> 00:04:01.984
Confirm decisive knockout results and advance the winners, through the configured rounds and final.

00:04:01.984 --> 00:04:04.248
Use the final's own best-of length.

00:04:04.248 --> 00:04:08.582
Resolve disputes and stale opponent dependencies before continuing.

00:04:08.582 --> 00:04:14.404
Current stage means the first unfinished stage in that category; Upcoming means an earlier

00:04:14.404 --> 00:04:16.021
stage remains unfinished.

00:04:16.021 --> 00:04:18.867
These badges do not advance players for you.

00:04:18.867 --> 00:04:23.977
When the knockout is settled and its final has an accepted decisive result, the

00:04:23.977 --> 00:04:25.206
stage is Completed.

00:04:25.206 --> 00:04:29.558
Set the tournament status to Completed separately in Overview and schedule.
